      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.79,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So we got this backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.79,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "and in order to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 8.1,
          "en": "we now have to start this backend API web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.1,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "Because again, it is a separate server, a separate project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "just integrated into this NextJS project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "for simplicity reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 20.31,
          "en": "So in your terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.31,
          "end": 22.83,
          "en": "you should make sure that you're in that backend folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.83,
          "end": 25.44,
          "en": "that you navigated there with the cd command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.44,
          "end": 28.53,
          "en": "and then you should run npm start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.53,
          "end": 32.733,
          "en": "to start that backend server and keep that up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "And then in a separate terminal window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "in a separate command-line window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "you should navigate into the root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "And then there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "run npm run dev to also start the NextJS server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "so that both servers are up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 55.2,
          "en": "The NextJS app is still served under this address here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 58.05,
          "en": "and the backend application will be served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 59.943,
          "en": "under localhost 8080.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 61.77,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.77,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "we can therefore now adjust our NextJS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 67.95,
          "en": "to fetch the news from the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.95,
          "end": 71.583,
          "en": "and the question now is how we would do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.51,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "Now, one way of fetching data from a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "from a separate API in a NextJS app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "like in any other React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.41,
          "en": "would be to do it on the client-side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 88.14,
          "en": "So here in the content route group,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.14,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "on the news page, for example, where we need our news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 94.17,
          "en": "instead of importing the Dummy_News",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.17,
          "end": 96.06,
          "en": "from the dummy-news file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.06,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "which we now assume doesn't exist anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "And instead now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "we're simulating that we have a real backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 106.92,
          "en": "with a real database that contains all that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.92,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "So instead of using that Dummy_News from that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 112.833,
          "en": "the goal now is to fetch the data from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 117.84,
          "en": "And we could do that here in that NewsPage component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.84,
          "end": 122.34,
          "en": "by using the fetch function that's built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "And we could use that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 125.76,
          "en": "with help of the useEffect Hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 129.27,
          "en": "which is how you typically would send requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.27,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "and handle side effects like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 134.67,
          "en": "such as HTTP request in React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.67,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "And you do learn about that in my separate React course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 143.01,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also use a third-party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.01,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "like TanStack Query, which I also cover in my React course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "to fetch data from some backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "and this package would then make this process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "of fetching data and also caching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 158.07,
          "en": "and so on a bit simpler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 160.07999999999998,
          "en": "But to keep the code simple here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "I will actually use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 164.34,
          "en": "the standard built-in fetch function here inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "of a useEffect function, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 170.76,
          "en": "to fetch data from a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "And then we can send a request to localhost 8080,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 176.1,
          "en": "which is the address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.1,
          "end": 179.04,
          "en": "of that separate backend server we started a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.04,
          "end": 180.63,
          "en": "of minutes ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.63,
          "end": 183.57,
          "en": "And then this will give us back a Promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.57,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "Now, it's not considered a good practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 189.9,
          "en": "to decorate this effect function with async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.9,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "in order to use async/await, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 194.99,
          "en": "I'll create a separate function in there, fetchNews,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.74,
          "end": 198.36,
          "en": "and move the fetch function in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.36,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "and decorate that with async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 202.98,
          "en": "so that we then can use await here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 202.98,
          "end": 205.02,
          "en": "And then outside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.02,
          "end": 207.36,
          "en": "but still inside of the effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 210.993,
          "en": "we can call fetchNews to trigger this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 215.14,
          "en": "Now what we'll get back is a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 218.52,
          "en": "and that response, of course, might fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.52,
          "end": 220.32,
          "en": "So we could check if (!response.ok),",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "so if we got an error or status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 228.18,
          "en": "in which case we might want to update some error or state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.18,
          "end": 230.673,
          "en": "so that we can show some error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "So we can add the useStatus Hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 236.553,
          "en": "to the NewsPage component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 240.87,
          "en": "and then manage some error state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.87,
          "end": 243.39,
          "en": "and set the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 246.93,
          "en": "if we got an erroneous response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.93,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "and maybe set this to a error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 252.933,
          "en": "like Failed to fetch news or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 257.1,
          "en": "If we make it past this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "we also might want to show some loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 261.57,
          "en": "whilst we're fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 261.57,
          "end": 264.603,
          "en": "so therefore, we could also add another state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.37,
          "end": 267.963,
          "en": "isLoading state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.88,
          "end": 273.13,
          "en": "which we wanna set to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 277.40999999999997,
          "en": "before we start sending that request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.40999999999997,
          "end": 279.723,
          "en": "And maybe set it to false initially here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.74,
          "end": 284.88,
          "en": "But if we got an error, we wanna set it to false again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 286.56,
          "en": "because even though we have an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.56,
          "end": 289.05,
          "en": "we're not loading data anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 291.45,
          "en": "And of course, if we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.45,
          "end": 295.35,
          "en": "we will have our news and we're also not loading anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.35,
          "end": 299.73,
          "en": "So here we also might want to set setIsLoading to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 303.603,
          "en": "and then introduce a third state into this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 309.66,
          "en": "a news state with a setNews updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.66,
          "end": 314.043,
          "en": "where we then set our news to the response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.88,
          "end": 317.55,
          "en": "And actually that data must be parsed first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.55,
          "end": 320.43,
          "en": "so our news from the backend can be retrieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.43,
          "end": 322.41,
          "en": "by calling response.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 324.93,
          "en": "and that will give us a Promise which we need to await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 324.93,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "So it's then those parsed news which we wanna set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 331.113,
          "en": "as our news state in that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 333.24,
          "end": 335.4,
          "en": "And with that, we would be sending a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 337.71,
          "en": "and handle those different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.71,
          "end": 340.44,
          "en": "And now of course, we should use these different states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 340.44,
          "end": 342.6,
          "en": "to update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 342.6,
          "end": 347.01,
          "en": "For example, we can check if we're loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.01,
          "end": 347.90999999999997,
          "en": "and in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 347.90999999999997,
          "end": 352.08299999999997,
          "en": "we might want to return a simple loading fallback like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 354.54,
          "end": 358.11,
          "en": "If we have an error, so if that is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 358.11,
          "end": 361.26,
          "en": "we might wanna return the error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 361.26,
          "end": 363.153,
          "en": "on the screen and show that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 364.95,
          "end": 367.86,
          "en": "And only if you make it past these two if checks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 367.86,
          "end": 370.62,
          "en": "only in that case, we wanna output the news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 370.62,
          "end": 374.07,
          "en": "though news might be undefined initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 374.07,
          "end": 377.4,
          "en": "because initially there is no news state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 377.4,
          "end": 379.08,
          "en": "and therefore we should also check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.08,
          "end": 381.15,
          "en": "whether we really have some news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 381.15,
          "end": 386.15,
          "en": "So the newsContent here initially is undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 387.03,
          "end": 389.34,
          "en": "and then we check if we have news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 389.34,
          "end": 392.58,
          "en": "in which case I'll set the newsContent variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 392.58,
          "end": 394.62,
          "en": "to that NewsList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 394.62,
          "end": 397.743,
          "en": "to which I passed the news, which I now know exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 399.03,
          "end": 401.79,
          "en": "And down here, we output the newsContent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 401.79,
          "end": 405.783,
          "en": "which is either nothing or that NewsList here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.52,
          "end": 411.09000000000003,
          "en": "And that is how we could fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 411.09000000000003,
          "end": 415.74,
          "en": "in our NextJS application when we have a separate backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 415.74,
          "end": 416.573,
          "en": "because of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 416.573,
          "end": 420.12,
          "en": "that is how we could fetch data in any React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 420.12,
          "end": 422.313,
          "en": "and NextJS is no exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 423.78,
          "end": 425.58,
          "en": "So with all that code added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 425.58,
          "end": 427.95,
          "en": "if we reload on that news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 427.95,
          "end": 431.37,
          "en": "we get an error that we're using useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 431.37,
          "end": 435.06,
          "en": "and that this only works in Client Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 435.06,
          "end": 439.35,
          "en": "because indeed the useEffect Hook is a hook that needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 439.35,
          "end": 441.99,
          "en": "to run on the client-side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 441.99,
          "end": 445.86,
          "en": "So therefore, we should add the use client directive here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 445.86,
          "end": 449.52,
          "en": "which of course is already a small disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 449.52,
          "end": 453.42,
          "en": "to what we had before when this was a Server Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 453.42,
          "end": 457.68,
          "en": "because now it's not a pure Server Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 457.68,
          "end": 458.67,
          "en": "And therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 458.67,
          "end": 461.1,
          "en": "we have to execute some code on the client-side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 461.1,
          "end": 463.40999999999997,
          "en": "which is not always a big problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 463.40999999999997,
          "end": 466.29,
          "en": "but which is less ideal than running all the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 466.29,
          "end": 467.463,
          "en": "on the server-side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 468.93,
          "end": 471.42,
          "en": "With that though, if we save that and we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 471.42,
          "end": 473.7,
          "en": "I get an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 473.7,
          "end": 476.79,
          "en": "So this error fallback is shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 476.79,
          "end": 479.55,
          "en": "because in the end I got a 404 error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 479.55,
          "end": 480.63,
          "en": "The reason for that simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 480.63,
          "end": 485.61,
          "en": "is that I'm sending my request just to the backend domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 485.61,
          "end": 490.08,
          "en": "but if we take a look at the backend code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 490.08,
          "end": 493.56,
          "en": "we can actually see that it is /news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 493.56,
          "end": 495.36,
          "en": "to which we should send the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 496.71,
          "end": 498.81,
          "en": "So therefore, we should adjust this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 498.81,
          "end": 499.983,
          "en": "and send it to /news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 501.45,
          "end": 504.15,
          "en": "And with that done, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 504.15,
          "end": 508.11,
          "en": "you can see the news are popping in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 508.11,
          "end": 511.38,
          "en": "And that's therefore one way of loading data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 511.38,
          "end": 513.39,
          "en": "in a NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 513.39,
          "end": 514.38,
          "en": "And of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 514.38,
          "end": 518.52,
          "en": "it is a way that we could use in any React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 518.52,
          "end": 519.353,
          "en": "and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 519.353,
          "end": 523.29,
          "en": "it's a generally absolutely fine way of loading data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 523.29,
          "end": 527.1,
          "en": "But it's not the best way of loading data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
